### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
Joe Biden explicitly denied wanting to ban fracking, stating in a Pittsburgh speech, “I am not banning fracking” [source](https://www.uagetinvolved.org/content/joe-biden-i-am-not-banning-fracking). His campaign clarified that his earlier “no new fracking” remark referred only to halting new drilling leases on federal lands, not a total ban [source](https://energynow.com/2020/09/the-biden-flip-flop-u-s-presidential-hopeful-biden-now-says-he-would-not-ban-fracking/). Running mate Kamala Harris also affirmed during the vice presidential debate that “Joe Biden will not end fracking” [source](https://www.api.org/news-policy-and-issues/blog/2020/10/09/joe-biden-will-not-ban-fracking). Additionally, the 2020 Democratic Party platform did not include a fracking ban [source](https://www.spglobal.com/commodityinsights/en/market-insights/latest-news/natural-gas/082520-republicans-warn-of-fracking-ban-oil-and-gas-jobs-loss-on-day-one-of-convention). All evidence directly contradicts the claim.